.TH "Docv::Viewer::Keymap" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Viewer::Keymap \- Maps key events to values of \fIT\fR: first by physical key (base layout), then by the reported key, then by the shifted symbol without its shift.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Viewer::Keymap(T)\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Maps key events to values of \fIT\fR: first by physical key (base layout),
then by the reported key, then by the shifted symbol without its
shift.
.SH "DIRECT KNOWN SUBCLASSES"
\fBDocv::Viewer::Bindings\fR,
\fBDocv::Viewer::FieldBindings\fR,
\fBDocv::Viewer::TreeBindings\fR
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(entries : Enumerable(Tuple(Term::Mods, Int32, T)))\fR
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef []=(binding : Tuple(Term::Mods, Int32), value : T) : T\fR
Binds \fImods\fR + \fIkey\fR to \fIvalue\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef keys(value : T) : Array(Tuple(Term::Mods, Int32))\fR
The bindings of \fIvalue\fR, in the order they were made.
.TP 4
\fBdef lookup(event : Term::KeyEvent) : T | Nil\fR
The value bound to \fIevent\fR, if any.
